WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:14.777
One million two hundred sixty-four thousand four hundred and sixty-seven government contracts analyzed from open dot canada dot ca. Seventy thousand two hundred and seventy anomalies detected — including fifty-seven vendor concentration flags and over seventy thousand amendment chains.

00:00:14.727 --> 00:00:18.579
Sole-source patterns identified across multiple departments.

00:00:18.579 --> 00:00:24.454
IBM Canada, Groupe Signature, and MDA Systems flagged as high-concentration vendors.

00:00:24.454 --> 00:00:31.261
Amendment chain exploits documented — contracts modified repeatedly to circumvent competitive procurement requirements.

00:00:31.261 --> 00:00:35.727
The Department of National Defence shows the highest anomaly concentration.

00:00:35.727 --> 00:00:46.079
Criminal Code sections 121, 380, and 418 — fraud on the government, fraud over five thousand dollars, and selling defective stores to the Crown.

00:00:46.079 --> 00:00:49.011
These are not theoretical legal risks.

00:00:49.011 --> 00:00:52.636
They map directly to the procurement patterns found in the data.
